<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Victor Emmanuel II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1820–1878</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Victor Emmanuel II was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> from 1849 and the first King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> from 1861. With his prime minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camillo-benso-count-of-cavour">Cavour</a> he allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> in 1859, ceding Savoy and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nice">Nice</a> to France in 1860, and annexed most of the peninsula. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venetia">Venetia</a> followed in 1866 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 1870, which became his capital.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/victor-emmanuel-ii.jpg" alt="Victor Emmanuel II" width="320" height="484" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eugène Disdéri · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:VictorEmmanuel2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
